## FOOTNOTE CITATION FORMAT (ACADEMIC STYLE)

**CRITICAL**: All footnotes MUST follow academic citation format:

```
Author. (Year, Month Day). Title. Publication, URL
```

### Examples:

**News article:**
```
[^1]: Invezz. (2025, October 14). Perp DEX Avantis transitions to unified vault. invezz.com, https://invezz.com/news/2025/10/14/perp-dex-avantis-transitions-unified-vault/
```

**API data source:**
```
[^2]: DefiLlama. (2025, December 31). Avantis TVL: $102.9M retrieved via API. defillama.com, https://defillama.com/protocol/avantis 🔷 HARD DATA
```

**Documentation:**
```
[^3]: Avantis. (2025). Official protocol documentation: Trading fees and vault mechanics. docs.avantis.fi, https://docs.avantis.fi/
```

**Educational source:**
```
[^4]: Phemex Academy. (2025). What is Avantis: Protocol overview and RWA markets. phemex.com, https://phemex.com/academy/what-is-avantis
```

### Format Rules:
1. **Author**: Organization name OR "Last, First Initial." for individuals
2. **Date**: (Year, Month Day) or (Year, Month) or (Year) or (Year, Quarter)
3. **Title**: Article/page title in sentence case
4. **Publication**: Domain without www or https
5. **URL**: Full URL at end, no square brackets

### DO NOT USE this old format:
```
❌ [^1]: [Source Name](URL) - Description
```

### ALWAYS USE academic format:
```
✅ [^1]: Author. (Year, Month Day). Title. publication.com, https://full-url.com
```

